    "content": "The Artemis II mission features a four-person crew—NASA astronauts Reid Wiseman (commander), Victor Glover (pilot), Christina Hammock Koch (mission specialist), and CSA astronaut Jeremy Hansen (mission specialist)—set for a 10-day lunar flyby mission. This crew will test the Orion spacecraft's systems in deep space, marking the first human return to the Moon's vicinity since 1970. Artemis II Crew Details: Reid Wiseman (Commander): A US Navy pilot and former Chief of the Astronaut Office, this is his second spaceflight. Victor Glover (Pilot): A US Navy aviator who served on the ISS, he will be the first Black person to travel to the Moon. Christina Hammock Koch (Mission Specialist): A NASA engineer holding the record for the longest single spaceflight by a woman; she is the first woman assigned to a lunar mission. Jeremy Hansen (Mission Specialist): A Canadian Space Agency (CSA) astronaut, he is the first non-US citizen to fly on a lunar mission. The mission is scheduled to fly farther from Earth than any previous human mission, testing the systems intended to support long-term exploration of the Moon and beyond.",
